.SS "uint32_t csmp::CSMP_ElementSpecifications::MinimumSpatialDimension (const std::string & etype)\fR [static]\fP"
The element type used defines the spatial dimension of the model\&. It is indicative only of the minimum dimension since lines and surfaces can also exist in 3D space, which the name makes explicit\&.
.SH "Input Arguments"
.PP
Method expects a std::string argument that contains the ANSYS element type to deduce the spatial dimension from\&.

.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
size_t The minimum spatial dimension is returned as an unsigned integer ranging from 1(=1D) to 3(=3D)\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "uint32_t csmp::CSMP_ElementSpecifications::NeighborsPerElementOfType (int8_t etype)\fR [static]\fP"
Returns the maximum possible number of neighbors of the input CSMP finite element type as specified in CSMP_FEM_conventions\&.pdf in the documentation directory\&. 
.SS "uint32_t csmp::CSMP_ElementSpecifications::NodesPerElementOfType (int8_t etype)\fR [static]\fP"
Returns the number of nodes of the CSMP element type as identified by the CSMP element integer code (enumeration \fBCSMP_FEM_TYPE\fP in \fBFiniteElement\&.h\fP)\&. 
.SS "uint32_t csmp::CSMP_ElementSpecifications::NodesPerFaceForElementOfType (int8_t etype, uint32_t face)\fR [static]\fP"
Returns number of nodes that make up a particular face of the supplied \fBCSMP_FEM_TYPE\fP enumeration as specified in \fBFiniteElement\&.h\fP

.PP
Use this method to retrieve this information before any finite elements have been built\&.

.PP
\fBAttention\fP
.RS 4
17/12/2015 SKM fixed method for quadratic elements 
.RE
.PP

